# --- Privy (required) ---------------------------------------------------
#
# Create an app at https://dashboard.privy.io and copy the values below from
# Settings. NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID is public by design (it is bundled into
# client JS). Do not put a secret in any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=

# Server-only. Dashboard -> Settings -> App secret. Required for
# app/api/wallet/ensure/route.ts (verifies access tokens and creates the
# embedded wallet that becomes the Kernel smart wallet's owner signer).
PRIVY_APP_SECRET=

# --- Privy dashboard checklist (settings live in your Privy app, not here) --
#
# Where each value comes from: https://dashboard.privy.io -> your app ->
# Settings (Basics). NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID is PUBLIC (bundled into client
# JS). PRIVY_APP_SECRET is SECRET and server-only; never prefix it NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# [ ] Allowed origins (Configuration -> App settings): add the exact origin
#     with the port, http://localhost:3000, plus your production domain
#     (https://your-domain). http://localhost without the port does not match,
#     and Next.js silently moves to 3001 if 3000 is busy; free the port.
# [ ] Login methods (User management -> Authentication): Google and email (matches loginMethods in
#     app/providers.tsx: google, email). Enable both.
#     Methods not enabled in the dashboard are hidden even if listed in code.
# [ ] Embedded wallets (Wallets): enable for Ethereum, create on login.
#     Coinbase eoaOnly is not relevant here (no external wallets offered).
#     WalletGate calls /api/wallet/ensure after login, which creates the wallet
#     server-side with PRIVY_APP_SECRET if the dashboard setting is off, so
#     both together is fine. TEE / user-controlled mode is what the live tests
#     used; the legacy device mode also works.
# [ ] Smart wallets (Wallets -> Smart wallets, may read Settings -> Wallet
#     infrastructure): REQUIRED for this template; it uses Privy Smart Wallets.
#       Enable it, then configure:
#         Provider:      Kernel (ZeroDev) v3.1
#         Custom chain:  PEPU, chainId 97741,
#                        RPC https://rpc-pepu-v2-mainnet-0.t.conduit.xyz
#         Bundler URL:   https://bundler.pepeunchained.com
#         Paymaster URL: https://paymaster.pepeunchained.com/v2/paymaster/<CLIENT token ppt_...>
#     Use the project CLIENT token (ppt_...) and add this app's origins to the
#     project's allowed origins, because Privy calls the URL from the browser.
#     NEVER put the server key (ppk_...) in the dashboard URL.
#     The free tier cannot be used on this path: a static dashboard URL carries
#     no per-user Privy token, so you need a funded project of your own.
#     Old dashboards may still hold temporary development bundler/paymaster
#     URLs (e.g. tunnels): replace them with the hosted ones above.
#
# Verify any time: npm run doctor (or the pepu_check_privy_config MCP tool).

# --- Paymaster (optional) ------------------------------------------------
#
# The deployed v2 paymaster (PepuSponsoredPaymasterV7 canary, external audit
# pending) contract address on PEPU mainnet.
# Not a secret: it is public on-chain information. This demo reads its
# EntryPoint deposit before and after a sponsored tap as the proof that
# sponsorship actually happened. Defaults to the address below if unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYMASTER_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=0xdb28528C9399C33c9A0297E8A62F39145acbC30D

# --- Before this demo can sponsor anything -------------------------------
#
# Sponsorship is configured entirely in the Privy Dashboard, not here.
# Settings -> Wallet infrastructure -> Smart wallets must have chain 97741,
# provider Kernel, and BOTH a bundler URL and a paymaster URL for that chain:
#
#   Bundler URL:   https://bundler.pepeunchained.com
#   Paymaster URL: https://paymaster.pepeunchained.com/v2/paymaster/<token>
#
# The paymaster URL always embeds a token for YOUR project (claim it, set
# targets and limits, deposit, register; see README.md). Use the project's
# CLIENT token (ppt_...) with this app's origins allowed, because Privy calls
# the URL from the browser. Never use the server key (ppk_...) here.
#
# The free tier (100 PEPU/day and 50 PEPU/hour per user, TapScore only for
# now) needs a Privy access token from PEPU's own Privy app in the ERC-7677
# context. Privy's dashboard URL cannot attach one, so it does not apply to
# this transport.
